---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy and cookies | Save My Gig!"
  description="What Save My Gig collects (very little), why, who processes it, and your rights."
  path="/privacy"
  noindex
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <div class="status-line">Privacy</div>
    <h1 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">PRIVACY, <span class="accent">PLAINLY</span></h1>

    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
      Short version: the rescue flow needs nothing from you. No account, no login, no files uploaded.
      Some free features (Pro and Custom checklists, the printable list, emailing yourself a copy)
      ask you to register with an email address. That address, plus two optional fields you can
      leave empty, is all the personal data we ever hold.
    </p>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Cookies and analytics</h3>
      <p class="dim">
        We use Google Analytics 4 to see which pages actually help and where people get stuck.
        It sets cookies, so we <strong>only load it after you accept</strong> on the banner.
        Decline and no analytics cookies are set, and the site works exactly the same.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        To change your mind later, clear this site's data in your browser and the banner will ask again.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">If you register</h3>
      <p class="dim">
        Registration collects your <strong>email address</strong> (required) and, only if you choose
        to share them, an <strong>artist name</strong> and an <strong>artist Instagram handle</strong>.
        The email is used to unlock the registered features, to send you what you asked for (your
        checklist, the Emergency Card), and for the occasional note that might save a gig or help
        your career. We use double opt-in for the mailing list: you get a confirmation email first,
        and nothing is added to the list until you click it.
      </p>
      <p class="dim">
        If you share your Instagram handle, we use it for exactly what the form says: to follow
        your work from the Save My Gig account. We also receive an internal notification email for
        each registration so we can do that. The optional fields are never required for any feature,
        and leaving them empty changes nothing.
      </p>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        This data is processed by <strong>Brevo</strong> (Sendinblue SAS, France), acting as our
        processor. We do not sell, rent or share it with anyone else. Every email has a one-click
        unsubscribe, and unsubscribing removes you. Your checklist itself (items, edits, ticks)
        is stored in your own browser on your own device, not on our servers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">Your rights</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        If you are in the EU or UK, you can ask us for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to
        correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to
        <a href="mailto:savemygig@gmail.com">savemygig@gmail.com</a> and we will action it.
        Our legal basis for the email list and the optional fields is your consent, which you can
        withdraw at any time; deleting your data removes your address, artist name and Instagram
        handle from our records. This applies worldwide, including under Brazil's LGPD: same
        address, same result.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">What we never do</h3>
      <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0">
        No selling of data. No tracking beyond the analytics
        described above. We never see your music, your files, or your drives.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:2rem">
      Last updated: July 2026 · Operated from Brazil · Contact:
      <a href="mailto:savemygig@gmail.com">savemygig@gmail.com</a> ·
      Some outbound links on the gear and recovery pages may become affiliate links; they never
      change what you pay and never appear inside the rescue flow.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
